mothershipOS: play with snd_pcm_writei (RW access) on the I/O path instead of alsa-lib's mmap emulation, which
0002 introduced for the DisplayPort dmix. With the PipeWire ALSA plugin (mship.audio: a VM's sound into its
PipeWire sink) the mmap path took one buffer (~300 ms) and then never saw room again: the guest's writes failed
("Error writing into ALSA") and the host got silence. writei is what ordinary ALSA clients (aplay) use, and works on
the dmix as well. A failed write is recovered (snd_pcm_recover) and retried in the next round.

--- a/src/audio_backends/alsa.rs
+++ b/src/audio_backends/alsa.rs
@@ -134,8 +134,7 @@
             })?;
 
             hwp.set_access(match s.direction {
-                Direction::Output => Access::MMapInterleaved,
-                Direction::Input => Access::RWInterleaved,
+                Direction::Output | Direction::Input => Access::RWInterleaved,
             })?;
 
             let frame_size = u32::from(s.params.channels)
@@ -318,35 +317,40 @@
         }
     };
